--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a derivative of KPConv-PyTorch and incorporates code from the
projects listed below. Each is distributed under its own licence, reproduced or
referenced here as required.

1. KPConv-PyTorch — Hugues Thomas
   https://github.com/HuguesTHOMAS/KPConv-PyTorch
   MIT License (Copyright (c) 2019 HuguesTHOMAS).
   This repository is derived from it; the network architecture, kernel point
   convolutions, dataset handling, training and testing pipeline originate there.

2. loss-landscape — Hao Li, Zheng Xu, Gavin Taylor, Christoph Studer, Tom Goldstein
   https://github.com/tomgoldstein/loss-landscape
   MIT License (Copyright (c) 2017 Hao Li, Zheng Xu, Gavin Taylor, Christoph Studer and Tom Goldstein).
   The filter-normalised weight perturbation approach used in diagnostics.py
   follows this work ("Visualizing the Loss Landscape of Neural Nets",
   NeurIPS 2018).

3. nanoflann — Jose Luis Blanco-Claraco and contributors
   https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann
   BSD 2-Clause License. The full licence text is retained in the header of
   cpp_wrappers/cpp_utils/nanoflann/nanoflann.hpp and must be kept intact.
